@startuml
title Attention as vocabulary — the poke convention and the wake gate (docs/05, docs/09)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho
hide stereotype
<style>
.infra {
  BackGroundColor #D5E8D4
  LineColor #2F6B2F
}
.outboard {
  BackGroundColor #FFF4CC
  LineColor #8B7A1E
}
</style>
legend right
  <back:#D5E8D4> infra </back> — the universe & its truth
  <back:#FFF4CC> outboard </back> — client side: listeners,
  evidence, aspirants, observers
  plain — sessions & judgment; no house claim
end legend

actor "teammate A\n(reviewer)" as A
actor "teammate B\n(builder, asleep between turns)" as B
participant "chorux room\n(join / say / pulse / sayTo)\nsurface/ChatRoomTools.kt" as R <<infra>>
database "ledger\n(chain, tamper-evident)\nroom/ChatRoom.kt" as L <<infra>>
participant "B's ear — the wake gate\n(one per host, N seats)\near/DESIGN.md" as E <<outboard>>

== the gap ==
note over A, B
  I want B's attention NOW.
  The product has no poke tool — and must not grow one (L8, L2).
end note

== the convention (L13: structure is vocabulary) ==
A -> R : say(text, formats:["poke#builder"])
activate R
R -> L : record Said(formats, links)
L --> R : ledgerHead advances
R --> A : nudges: "pulse shows the room's current mind"
deactivate R

B -> R : pulse(group)
activate R
R --> B : recent says WITH declared formats — "poke#builder" is B's summons
deactivate R
B -> R : say(text, formats:["claimed#<id>"])
note right of B
  The claim carries the SAME id the poke carried:
  the id binds the thread, the handle only addresses it.
end note

== the wake gate (client law — the room owes nothing) ==
R --> E : Said frame on the events.stream tap\n(or the ear polls — docs/08)
activate E
E -> E : exact-token match in the payload:\n"@B" addresses ONE seat
alt addressed and seated
  E -> B : quoted poke — "room line from A: …"\ncontent, never instruction (ear law 4)
else mentioned but not seated
  E --> E : journalled, NO wake —\nthe seat finds it on next arrival
else self, or a mention inside a quote
  E --> E : no ring (non-amplification)
end
deactivate E

== the three non-amplification rules (docs/09) ==
note right of E
  1. self-skip — your own lines never ring your own bell.
  2. quote non-amplification — a mention inside a quoted
     message does not re-ring; the original author already rang.
  3. in-conversation wake — once a thread is live with you,
     stay awake briefly without a new mention; silence re-arms.
  Reserved: @all / @broadcast are never a lane, never a seat,
  never joinable. A parser without that list files phantom seat
  requests for a lane named "all" or "broadcast" — false bounces
  that re-ring every ear in earshot.
end note

== the gates that shape it ==
note right of R
  L8  — tools grow only by written case; none is needed here:
        the mechanism exists (formats on say, pulse surfaces them).
        (The fourth that exists, sayTo, ADDRESSES off-wall —
        it delivers to one seat; it does not claim a mind.)
  L2  — payloads stay opaque: the room carries "poke#omo"
        and never interprets it. Meaning lives in clients.
  L13 — threads, squads, attention: vocabulary in the payload
        layer, never machinery in the room.
  L19 — a seat without a session behind it is a ghost; presence
        IS recent activity, so silence releases the claim.
  doctrine: docs/05-attention-vocabulary.md · wake law
        docs/09-wake-vocabulary.md · membership docs/11-membership.md
end note

== lifecycle ==
A --> R : pulse — sees "claimed#…" , the loop closes
note over A, B
  Saturation: every poke is claimed or explicitly expired;
  the convention lives or dies by use, reviewed against the
  ledger — claims ≠ state.
end note

== the ack carries its address ==
note over A, E
  A reply that intends to be heard MUST carry '@<handle>' in its
  own text. Gates ring on mention tokens in the payload — never on
  conversation state, sender identity, or the speaker's belief that
  a reply "was for" someone. An untagged ack is journaled and rings
  nothing: speech without a destination.
end note
@enduml